corrected residue (1,183,214,875 bytes) sits below the unchanged alarm threshold; ACs prove only that the calculation is now commensurable.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f59b3078b5ae2458a","impact":0.55,"is_primary":null,"location":"Acceptance criteria AC5 / title","norm_id":"n5e8acabba7030a02","priority":0.1375,"reason":"veto:absence-refuted","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Corrected metric still exceeds the existing threshold and the alarm keeps false-firing despite the fix"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"State the current threshold value and add an assertion/observation that 1,183,214,875 bytes is below it (with headroom), or document why the threshold remains appropriate post-fix.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.25,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"no","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"no","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"underspecified_oracle","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"none","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"underspecified_certification","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"none","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"none","reversibility":"easy","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"none"}}},{"block_threshold":0.95,"blocking_enabled":false,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify in the Design why a hand-rolled `find -xdev`/`stat` traversal is chosen over the established `du` (e.g. state that a single GNU du invocation cannot emit both allocated and apparent totals in one traversal, forcing either two du walks or one custom pass), or adopt du if it can serve.","cohort":["A1"],"criteria":["A1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.851,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Existing impl uses du: observability.sh:805 `du -x --block-size=1 --max-depth=1 \"$root\"`, and the surrounding comments (observability.sh:425-426, 806-808) already rely on du's single-run hardlink counting and --max-depth=1 subtotal.","Plan Design: 'hardlinks are de-duplicated by device+inode so allocated/apparent totals retain du-like semantics' — explicitly reimplementing behavior du provides natively.","Plan Design: 'This avoids the rejected second du walk from bug 9313' — this justifies avoiding a second walk, not the choice of find/stat over du for the single remaining walk.","The plausible affirmative reason (a single GNU du invocation cannot emit both allocated and apparent totals at once) is not stated anywhere in the plan."],"finding":"The Design replaces the existing `du` census with a hand-rolled `find -xdev`/`stat` traversal that reimplements du's own capabilities (allocated blocks via block-size, apparent size via --apparent-size, and within-run hardlink de-duplication) without justifying why du — the established tool already in use — cannot serve. The only rationale given ('avoids the rejected second du walk from bug 9313') argues against a SECOND walk, not against using du for the ONE remaining walk.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f0b6b12a041794c90","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Plan §Design (bullets on find -xdev / st_blocks*512 / st_size / hardlink de-dup)","norm_id":"neb5d6bb5deb1fb76","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["A reviewer or future maintainer asks why the proven `du` tool was abandoned for hand-rolled find/stat + awk hardlink bookkeeping that must re-verify du-equivalence.","The hand-rolled dedup introduces a subtle divergence from du semantics that the bug-9313/storage tests were written against."],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add one Design sentence: a single `du` run emits either allocated (`--block-size=1`) or apparent (`--apparent-size`) totals but not both, so obtaining both in one budget-bounded Docker-root traversal requires a single find/stat pass; du's within-run hardlink de-dup is therefore replicated via device+inode keying to keep du-equivalent semantics.","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":"na","current_state_satisfies_plan_goal":"na","evidence_entails_finding":"no","impact_follows_necessarily":"no","is_verifiable":"yes","no_existing_mitigation":"no","no_viable_alternative_explanation":"no","path_reachable":"yes","prerequisite_attribution_valid":"na","respects_artifact_altitude":"yes","severity_claim_justified":"no"},"severity_attributes":{"ac_unverifiable":"none","blast_radius":"local","debt_impact":"medium","divergent_implementation":"none","dod_uncertifiable":"none","internal_conflict":"none","irreversible_without_rationale":"low","likelihood":"low","prod_impact":"low","reversibility":"moderate","silent_vs_self_revealing":"self_revealing","undecomposed":"none","vague_directive":"low"}}},{"block_threshold":0.7,"blocking_enabled":true,"checklist_item":"- [ ] Justify reimplementing du's hardlink-dedup and dual allocated/apparent accounting in a find/stat pass versus using du's own `--apparent-size` mode (e.g., within the single-walk budget), or record why du prior art was rejected for the new apparent-size minuend.","cohort":["T1"],"criteria":["T1"],"decision":"dropped","decision_margin":-0.601,"drop_reason":null,"evidence":["Design: 'allocated bytes = sum of st_blocks * 512 ... apparent bytes = sum of st_size ... hardlinks are de-duplicated by device+inode so allocated/apparent totals retain du-like semantics'","AC3: 'obtains allocated and apparent Docker-root sizes from one filesystem traversal, not two du walks or root+overlay2 walks'","observability.sh:805 current mechanism is `du -x --block-size=1 --max-depth=1` — the plan replaces du entirely rather than using `du --apparent-size` for the new minuend","No occurrence of 'apparent' or '--apparent-size' in observability.sh (search returned no matches), confirming du's apparent-size mode is not referenced as prior art"],"finding":"The design hand-rolls du-equivalent semantics (hardlink de-duplication by device+inode, and dual allocated/apparent totals) in a find -xdev + stat traversal without acknowledging that GNU du already provides these natively — including `du --apparent-size` for the st_size sum and built-in hardlink dedup — so the anti-repackaging basis for reimplementing them in shell is unstated.","group_criteria":null,"group_id":null,"id":"f3069a6f936c4f271","impact":0.264,"is_primary":null,"location":"Design section (single-traversal find/stat pass); AC3","norm_id":"nc46520ff18be63b2","priority":0.099,"reason":"low-validity","recalled":false,"scenarios":["Reviewer/maintainer asks why du (which already dedupes hardlinks and has --apparent-size) was reimplemented in find/stat, risking subtle divergence from du semantics the plan claims to preserve","A find/stat pipeline mis-handles a device+inode edge case that du's mature implementation already handles, silently drifting from du-like totals"],"severity":null,"suggested_fix":"Add a sentence to the Design noting du's `--apparent-size` and native hardlink dedup as the prior art, and state why a find -xdev + stat traversal is preferred over it (e.g., single walk yields allocated + apparent + overlay2 subtotal together within the bug-9313 timeout budget, which two du invocations would blow).","tier":"LLM","validity":0.375,"verification":{"binary":{"absence_confirmed_in_context":"yes","asserted_capability_confirmed":"na","cited_reference_accurate":"yes","claims_absence":"yes","committed_work_relies_on_unbacked_claim":